            ("What marble memorial in Washington D.C. features a 19-foot seated statue of Abraham Lincoln looking out over the Reflecting Pool?", "The Lincoln Memorial", ["The Jefferson Memorial", "The Washington Monument", "The FDR Memorial"], "Designed by Henry Bacon, the temple features the text of the Gettysburg Address and Lincoln's Second Inaugural Address."),
            ("What 555-foot marble obelisk on the National Mall in Washington D.C. was built to commemorate the first President of the United States?", "The Washington Monument", ["The Jefferson Memorial", "The Lincoln Memorial", "The World War II Memorial"], "Engineered by Robert Mills, it was the tallest structure in the world when completed in 1884."),
            ("What circular neoclassical memorial on the Tidal Basin in Washington D.C. features a bronze statue of the author of the Declaration of Independence?", "The Thomas Jefferson Memorial", ["The Lincoln Memorial", "The Washington Monument", "The Madison Memorial"], "Surrounded by famous Japanese cherry blossom trees, the memorial features engraved excerpts from Jefferson's political writings."),
            ("What national military cemetery in Virginia across the Potomac River from Washington D.C. contains the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier?", "Arlington National Cemetery", ["Gettysburg National Cemetery", "Colonial National Historical Cemetery", "Quantico National Cemetery"], "Established on the former plantation of Robert E. Lee during the Civil War, Arlington serves as the final resting place for over 400,000 veterans."),
            ("What memorial in Arlington National Cemetery is guarded 24 hours a day, 365 days a year by elite sentinels of the 3rd US Infantry Regiment (The Old Guard)?", "The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier", ["The Eternal Flame", "The Space Shuttle Challenger Memorial", "The USS Maine Memorial"], "Dedicated in 1921, the tomb honors unidentified American military personnel who made the ultimate sacrifice in wartime."),
            ("What historic gravesite in Arlington National Cemetery features an Eternal Flame lit by Jacqueline Kennedy in 1963?", "Gravesite of President John F. Kennedy", ["Gravesite of General George C. Marshall", "Gravesite of Robert F. Kennedy", "Gravesite of General John J. Pershing"], "The gravesite overlooks Washington D.C., visited by millions of citizens paying tribute to the 35th President."),
            ("What V-shaped black granite reflective memorial in Washington D.C., designed by Maya Lin, is etched with over 58,000 names of fallen service members?", "The Vietnam Veterans Memorial", ["The Korean War Veterans Memorial", "The World War I Memorial", "The National World War II Memorial"], "Unveiled in 1982, the reflective black wall lists names chronologically by date of casualty, creating an intensely moving emotional tribute."),
            ("What memorial on the National Mall consists of 19 stainless steel statues depicting an infantry squad advancing through rice paddies in ponchos?", "The Korean War Veterans Memorial", ["The Vietnam Veterans Memorial", "The World War II Memorial", "The Marine Corps War Memorial"], "The memorial honors service members who fought in the Korean War (1950-1953), bearing the inscription 'Freedom Is Not Free.'"),
            ("What iconic bronze monument in Arlington, Virginia depicts five Marines and a Navy corpsman raising the American flag on Mount Suribachi during WWII?", "The Marine Corps War Memorial (Iwo Jima Memorial)", ["The Navy Memorial", "The National D-Day Memorial", "The Air Force Memorial"], "Sculpted by Felix de Weldon based on Joe Rosenthal's Pulitzer Prize-winning photograph, it honors all Marines who gave their lives."),
            ("What is the formal constitutional duty required of every male United States citizen within 30 days of turning 18 years old?", "Register with the Selective Service System", ["Register with a political party", "Obtain a federal passport", "Pay federal property tax"], "Federal law requires virtually all male US citizens and male immigrants residing in the US to register with Selective Service upon turning 18."),
            ("What fundamental civic responsibility is expected of every United States citizen summoned to participate in the judicial trial process?", "Serving on a jury when summoned", ["Running for elected public office", "Writing letters to congressional representatives", "Donating to campaign finance committees"], "Jury service ensures that accused individuals are judged by an impartial community of their peers, upholding constitutional due process."),
            ("What civic obligation requires citizens who earn taxable income above statutory thresholds to file annual returns with the federal government?", "Filing and paying federal income taxes", ["Purchasing municipal bonds", "Volunteering for civil defense duties", "Voting in every state referendum"], "Tax revenue finances national defense, public infrastructure, education, Medicare, Social Security, and federal government services."),
            ("What voluntary civic act is the cornerstone of democratic self-governance in the United States?", "Voting in federal, state, and local elections", ["Serving in the armed forces", "Joining a labor union", "Attending municipal zoning board hearings"], "Voting empowers citizens to elect representatives, shape government policies, and hold political leaders accountable.")
