            ("What historical geographical landmark in Greenwich, London, England represents the Prime Meridian (0 degrees longitude)?", "The Royal Observatory, Greenwich", ["Big Ben clock tower", "Westminster Abbey", "Tower of London"], "Established in 1884, the Prime Meridian divides the Eastern and Western Hemispheres and anchors Greenwich Mean Time (GMT)."),
