            ("What is the largest species of sea turtle, possessing an inky-blue flexible leathery carapace rather than a hard bony shell?", "The Leatherback Sea Turtle (Dermochelys coriacea)", ["The Green Sea Turtle", "The Loggerhead Sea Turtle", "The Hawksbill Sea Turtle"], "Leatherbacks can weigh up to 1,500 pounds and dive to depths of 4,000 feet hunting deep-water jellyfish."),
            ("What species of tree, native to the Sierra Nevada mountains of California, is the largest single tree on Earth by wood volume?", "The Giant Sequoia (Sequoiadendron giganteum)", ["The Coast Redwood", "The Douglas Fir", "The Montezuma Cypress"], "The 'General Sherman' giant sequoia in Sequoia National Park contains over 52,500 cubic feet of wood."),
            ("What species of tree, growing along the foggy Pacific coast of northern California, is the tallest living tree on Earth?", "The Coast Redwood (Sequoia sempervirens)", ["The Giant Sequoia", "The Sitka Spruce", "The Mountain Ash"], "The tallest living tree, a coast redwood named 'Hyperion', stands at an astounding 380 feet (115.8 meters) tall."),
