            ("What natural phenomenon causes the colorful glowing displays of light in high-latitude night skies known as the Aurora Borealis?", "Collisions between energetic charged solar wind particles and gas atoms (oxygen and nitrogen) in Earth's upper atmosphere", ["Refraction of moonlight through suspended high-altitude ice crystals", "Electrical discharges between volcanic ash clouds", "Spontaneous combustion of atmospheric methane gas"], "Earth's magnetic field funnels solar electrons toward the polar ionosphere, exciting oxygen (green/red) and nitrogen (blue/violet)."),
            ("What scale developed by Charles Richter in 1935 historically quantified the seismic energy released by earthquakes on a logarithmic scale?", "The Richter Magnitude Scale", ["The Modified Mercalli Intensity Scale", "The Fujita Scale", "The Saffir-Simpson Scale"], "Each whole-number increase on the logarithmic scale represents a roughly 32-fold increase in seismic energy release."),
