            ("What meteorological scale categorizes Atlantic hurricanes from Category 1 to Category 5 based on sustained wind speeds?", "The Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind Scale", ["The Enhanced Fujita Scale", "The Beaufort Scale", "The Torro Scale"], "Category 1 begins at 74 mph, and Category 5 catastrophic hurricanes feature sustained winds of 157 mph or higher."),
            ("What meteorological scale rates tornado intensity from EF0 to EF5 based on estimated wind speeds and post-storm structural damage?", "The Enhanced Fujita Scale (EF Scale)", ["The Saffir-Simpson Scale", "The Beaufort Scale", "The Richter Scale"], "EF0 causes light damage (65-85 mph); violent EF5 tornadoes exceed 200 mph, sweeping away sturdy frame houses."),
            ("What empirical scale measures wind speed based on observable effects on ocean waves and land objects, ranging from 0 (Calm) to 12 (Hurricane)?", "The Beaufort Wind Scale", ["The Fujita Scale", "The Saffir-Simpson Scale", "The Mach Scale"], "Devised in 1805 by Sir Francis Beaufort of the Royal Navy, it standardizes naval wind speed observations."),
            ("What mineral hardness scale ranks minerals from 1 (softest: talc) to 10 (hardest: diamond) based on scratch resistance?", "The Mohs Hardness Scale", ["The Brinell Hardness Scale", "The Rockwell Hardness Scale", "The Vickers Hardness Scale"], "Devised by Friedrich Mohs in 1812, minerals higher on the scale (e.g., quartz = 7, corundum = 9) scratch softer minerals."),
            ("What is the hardest known naturally occurring mineral on planet Earth, scoring a perfect 10 on the Mohs scale?", "Diamond (carbon crystal)", ["Corundum", "Topaz", "Quartz"], "The tetrahedral covalent carbon lattice gives diamond unmatched hardness and high thermal conductivity."),
